WEBVTT

00:10.176 --> 00:11.636
It'll be fine.

00:12.345 --> 00:13.846
He's gonna beat the shit outta me.

00:13.847 --> 00:15.889
I said, it'll be fine.

00:15.890 --> 00:17.726
I'm gonna get the belt.

00:18.351 --> 00:20.228
No, you're not.

00:20.770 --> 00:21.771
I will.

00:25.316 --> 00:27.402
Just go to your room, and stay there.

01:05.607 --> 01:07.400
I'm back on patrol in 30 minutes.

01:07.901 --> 01:10.320
So, talk fast. What happened?

01:11.696 --> 01:13.197
You know what happened.

01:13.198 --> 01:15.033
Yeah, well, I wanna hear it from you.

01:18.536 --> 01:20.454
I was buying pot from this other kid.

01:20.455 --> 01:22.499
He tried to rip me off,
and we got into a fight.

01:23.792 --> 01:25.793
That's what you're going with?

01:25.794 --> 01:27.211
- Okay.
- I'm telling the truth.

01:27.212 --> 01:29.588
No. No, you're not.

01:29.589 --> 01:31.465
I think Tommy
was buying the drugs, not you.

01:31.466 --> 01:33.842
I think you happened to walk by,
saw what was going on,

01:33.843 --> 01:35.969
- and started punching.
- Tommy didn't do anyth--

01:35.970 --> 01:37.763
I talked to the kid you beat up, Joel,

01:37.764 --> 01:39.348
and the officers
who got called to the scene.

01:39.349 --> 01:40.600
I'm not stupid.

01:41.684 --> 01:44.854
And if you and Tommy weren't my sons,
you'd both be in juvie right now.

01:48.066 --> 01:49.442
You're not gonna hurt him.

02:23.351 --> 02:26.980
Did I ever tell you
about that time I stole a candy bar?

02:29.065 --> 02:30.358
I was

02:30.900 --> 02:32.110
ten.

02:33.403 --> 02:37.949
Grandpa found out, made me give it back,
made me apologize to the cashier.

02:38.950 --> 02:40.868
And then, we went home.

02:40.869 --> 02:44.038
Just before I got out of the car,
man, he just...

02:46.291 --> 02:50.669
He broke my jaw.
There was blood everywhere.

02:50.670 --> 02:52.130
Grandma thought I was dead.

02:54.465 --> 02:56.843
My mouth was wired shut for two months.

02:58.178 --> 03:02.307
Everybody knew why.
It was humiliating.

03:04.058 --> 03:06.727
If you know what it feels like, then why?

03:06.728 --> 03:09.314
That's not why I'm telling you this.

03:10.690 --> 03:12.400
Okay, yeah, I've hit you.

03:13.735 --> 03:14.903
And I've hit Tommy.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.199
But never like that.

03:20.200 --> 03:21.783
Not even close.

03:21.784 --> 03:23.786
I mean, maybe I go too far, I...

03:25.121 --> 03:26.831
I don't know, I just...

03:28.958 --> 03:29.959
I don't know.

03:33.880 --> 03:36.007
But I'm doing a little better
than my father did.

03:42.096 --> 03:43.890
And you know, when it's your turn,

03:47.435 --> 03:49.020
I hope you do a little better than me.

05:46.721 --> 05:47.971
The new guy.

05:47.972 --> 05:50.098
Been here two months, Seth.

05:50.099 --> 05:52.935
Like I said. Got somethin' for me?

05:57.190 --> 05:58.358
I'll be fucked.

06:02.820 --> 06:04.821
My grandkids are gonna love these.

06:04.822 --> 06:05.989
How'd you find 'em?

06:05.990 --> 06:08.409
Searched the old homes out by Hoback.

06:09.410 --> 06:10.744
I searched those homes.

06:10.745 --> 06:14.207
Well, I know where to look
'cause I'm a smuggler, and you're a...

06:15.541 --> 06:16.918
I wasn't always this.

06:24.342 --> 06:25.510
I was a cop.

06:26.511 --> 06:27.804
Milwaukee PD.

06:33.434 --> 06:36.396
So, a trade's a trade.

06:37.105 --> 06:39.357
We can make what you want
and have it to you by

06:40.066 --> 06:41.359
Friday.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.070
No, I need it by tomorrow.

06:47.907 --> 06:50.410
Vanilla or chocolate?
Say vanilla, it's easier.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.161
Vanilla.

06:53.329 --> 06:54.664
Oh, I need one more thing.

06:55.665 --> 06:57.667
Relax. You got a lot of 'em.

08:26.672 --> 08:28.132
Joel!

08:32.970 --> 08:36.264
- What happened?
- Where'd you come from?

08:36.265 --> 08:37.682
Painkillers, she's alright.
Come on.

08:37.683 --> 08:39.559
- Painkillers?
- No, no, no.

08:39.560 --> 08:41.895
No, no, no, leave it.
Leave it, don't touch it.

08:41.896 --> 08:43.438
Tommy, what happened?

08:43.439 --> 08:45.774
She was working KP and she burned her arm.

08:45.775 --> 08:46.943
Well, how?

08:47.693 --> 08:49.611
I pushed it right up against a pot.

08:49.612 --> 08:50.905
You did this on purpose?

08:51.948 --> 08:54.950
I was like, "Here we go,"
and then I fucking went.

08:54.951 --> 08:58.245
- What? Why?
- No one saw. I was on my own.

08:58.246 --> 09:02.040
And I took it off and it was all red
and melting and gross.

09:02.041 --> 09:04.669
You know what it smelled like?
Pork.

09:05.211 --> 09:07.337
- Who let this happen?
- What do you mean, "let"?

09:07.338 --> 09:09.673
Who saw this comin'?
I was eating my damn dinner.

09:09.674 --> 09:10.925
- Oh, it hurts.
- Okay.

09:11.801 --> 09:12.801
Easy, baby girl.

09:12.802 --> 09:15.136
- Easy, easy.
- Dr. V ran over to the clinic.

09:15.137 --> 09:17.347
He's gonna come by here with another shot.

09:17.348 --> 09:18.933
Ellie.

09:21.894 --> 09:25.106
I just really wanted to wear
short sleeves again.

09:26.023 --> 09:28.526
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

09:29.485 --> 09:30.528
It's okay.

09:31.737 --> 09:33.406
It's okay. You're okay.

10:11.152 --> 10:13.529
- Goddammit, Seth.
- Hey.

10:16.490 --> 10:17.491
Hey.

10:20.453 --> 10:23.664
"Happy 15th Birthday, Eli."

10:26.459 --> 10:30.379
Well, let's hope Seth
bakes better than he spells.

10:33.215 --> 10:34.216
He does.

10:35.801 --> 10:37.595
It's really good.

10:41.766 --> 10:42.767
Oh, right.

10:43.976 --> 10:44.976
Stay right there.

10:44.977 --> 10:47.855
I got somethin' else for you.
Close your eyes.

10:50.524 --> 10:52.234
Keep 'em closed.

10:54.737 --> 10:56.364
Okay, turn toward me.

10:59.283 --> 11:01.577
And, open.

11:03.245 --> 11:05.915
- What's this?
- Some folks call this a "gee-tar."

11:07.416 --> 11:11.504
I borrowed one of your drawings
for inspiration.

11:13.047 --> 11:16.216
Took a bit of restorin'.
Real bone saddle here.

11:16.217 --> 11:20.845
Lacquered the whole body
and used a Dremel to carve the...

11:20.846 --> 11:23.556
Well, that's a rotary drill.
Or could be a saw, dependin' on the tip.

11:23.557 --> 11:26.727
But, actually,
it's a pretty versatile tool.

11:30.439 --> 11:31.440
Anyway.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.111
I had promised I would teach you, so.

11:36.362 --> 11:39.073
Well, if you want a lesson later.

11:39.824 --> 11:41.075
Let me hear something.

11:42.993 --> 11:45.245
- What do you mean, play it?
- And sing.

11:45.246 --> 11:48.748
No. No, no, no, no.
No, I don't sing.

11:48.749 --> 11:52.044
It's my fucking birthday, man.
Let's see what you got.

12:11.188 --> 12:12.231
Shit.

12:33.127 --> 12:37.464
If I ever were to lose you

12:37.465 --> 12:40.634
I'd surely lose myself

12:42.052 --> 12:46.014
Everything that I have found dear

12:46.015 --> 12:49.059
I've not found by myself

12:50.186 --> 12:53.606
Try and sometimes you'll succeed

12:54.648 --> 12:57.526
To make this man of me

12:58.903 --> 13:02.614
All my stolen, missing parts

13:02.615 --> 13:05.868
I've no need for anymore

13:07.620 --> 13:09.789
I believe

13:11.832 --> 13:15.920
And I believe 'cause I can see

13:17.087 --> 13:20.132
Our future days

13:21.133 --> 13:24.094
Days of you and me

13:29.600 --> 13:30.684
Well,

13:31.352 --> 13:32.770
that didn't suck.

13:53.666 --> 13:54.917
I understand.

13:57.586 --> 13:58.587
Your arm.

14:00.589 --> 14:01.757
I understand.

14:07.304 --> 14:08.806
Happy birthday, kiddo.

14:19.984 --> 14:22.235
- Is it a bow and arrow?
- Nope.

14:22.236 --> 14:24.445
Is it water guns?

14:24.446 --> 14:27.991
- No.
- Is it a dinosaur!

14:27.992 --> 14:30.493
- You're not gonna guess.
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

14:30.494 --> 14:32.036
Is it a "lotter" of kittens?

14:32.037 --> 14:33.372
A "lotter"?

14:34.498 --> 14:35.665
You mean a litter?

14:35.666 --> 14:37.750
A litter of kittens? Really?

14:37.751 --> 14:40.295
- Really. And no.
- Fuck.

14:40.296 --> 14:41.754
Is it a convertible?

14:41.755 --> 14:43.631
The hell are you gonna do
with a convertible?

14:43.632 --> 14:45.759
- Drive it.
- We cross here.

14:51.390 --> 14:52.808
How do you even know where we are?

14:54.018 --> 14:55.269
I found it on patrol.

14:56.437 --> 14:59.772
You know, Jesse was 16
when he started going on patrols.

14:59.773 --> 15:01.482
- Is that right?
- Don't get me wrong.

15:01.483 --> 15:04.569
I love counting vegetables
and shoveling sheep shit.

15:04.570 --> 15:06.988
I'm just saying,
I think I could be more useful

15:06.989 --> 15:08.156
outside the wall.

15:08.157 --> 15:10.533
You'll get on patrols eventually.

15:10.534 --> 15:13.578
You should enjoy being a kid for now.

15:13.579 --> 15:15.997
Oh, because childhood
has been such a joy for me so far.

15:15.998 --> 15:18.583
You've been 16 all of four hours.

15:18.584 --> 15:20.460
We're not sending you out
until you're trained.

15:20.461 --> 15:23.087
You're gonna need
somethin' called patience.

15:23.088 --> 15:24.924
Jesse said he'd train me if you let him.

15:26.008 --> 15:27.593
Is there somethin'
going on between you two?

15:28.802 --> 15:30.053
Excuse me?

15:30.054 --> 15:31.847
You spend a lot of time together.

15:33.015 --> 15:34.099
Is it funny?

15:34.642 --> 15:38.687
I see the way you look at him.
I got a keen eye for these sort of things.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.564
- I don't think you do.
- Alright, none of my business.

15:41.565 --> 15:44.484
But has anyone talked to you
about the birds and the bees?

15:44.485 --> 15:46.736
You mean dicks and vaginas?

15:46.737 --> 15:49.155
- Jesus.
- I tell you what.

15:49.156 --> 15:53.576
I promise you, I won't get pregnant
if you let me train for patrols. Deal?

15:53.577 --> 15:56.079
I'll see what I can do.

15:56.080 --> 15:57.581
Okay, how much longer, man?

15:58.749 --> 16:00.292
We're here.

16:10.970 --> 16:12.136
Oh, my God.

16:12.137 --> 16:14.430
It is a dinosaur!

16:14.431 --> 16:15.766
- Joel!
- Like it?

16:17.101 --> 16:19.144
Yeah. Likes it.

16:27.236 --> 16:28.237
Ellie.

16:29.154 --> 16:30.239
Ellie!

16:32.700 --> 16:35.077
Oh, my God. Careful.

16:36.787 --> 16:39.873
I'm on a motherfucking dinosaur!

16:42.668 --> 16:44.293
- Joel, there's a museum!
- Yeah, I know!

16:44.294 --> 16:46.337
If you don't fall off the goddamn T-Rex,

16:46.338 --> 16:47.589
I'll take you there.

16:56.807 --> 16:59.518
This is so cool.

17:00.936 --> 17:03.521
How long have you known about this place?

17:03.522 --> 17:04.939
A while.

17:04.940 --> 17:07.442
Well, then what the fuck?

17:07.443 --> 17:09.610
I was saving it for a special day.

17:09.611 --> 17:12.655
You see? Patience.

17:12.656 --> 17:14.575
Oh, yeah, I've heard of that.

17:50.360 --> 17:51.652
It works?

17:51.653 --> 17:53.447
Somebody must have greased it.

18:02.164 --> 18:04.208
Can you imagine being up there?

18:06.835 --> 18:08.962
- Would you like to?
- Like to what?

18:09.963 --> 18:11.006
Go to space?

18:28.482 --> 18:30.316
Is it real?

18:30.317 --> 18:31.400
It's real.

18:31.401 --> 18:33.278
That one went up and back.

18:34.113 --> 18:36.281
Apollo 15, 1971.

18:53.423 --> 18:54.591
Well, open it.

19:04.518 --> 19:05.894
You got it.

19:10.107 --> 19:12.024
You're going up to space.

19:12.025 --> 19:13.402
You need a helmet.

19:21.410 --> 19:22.494
Pick one.

20:04.203 --> 20:06.120
How's it smell in there?

20:06.121 --> 20:08.998
Like space, and dust.

20:08.999 --> 20:11.293
Well, good. Then, you're ready.

20:39.363 --> 20:42.449
People of Discovery, set! Abort!

20:47.788 --> 20:49.623
They sat right here.

20:54.336 --> 20:57.338
- Happy birthday, kiddo.
- What's this?

20:57.339 --> 21:01.968
This is something that took
a mighty effort to find.

21:01.969 --> 21:03.178
Play it.

21:19.987 --> 21:21.779
Close your eyes.

21:21.780 --> 21:23.490
It'll be worth it.

21:28.787 --> 21:31.580
Thirty seconds and counting.

21:31.581 --> 21:35.335
Astronauts report it feels good.
T-minus 25 seconds.

21:38.547 --> 21:40.173
Twenty seconds and counting.

21:42.342 --> 21:45.761
T-minus 15 seconds. Guidance is internal.

21:45.762 --> 21:49.640
Twelve, eleven, ten, nine.

21:49.641 --> 21:51.476
Ignition sequence starts.

21:52.853 --> 21:56.147
Six, five, four, three,

21:56.148 --> 21:58.816
two, one, zero.

21:58.817 --> 22:00.694
All engines running.

22:01.570 --> 22:03.696
Liftoff! We have a liftoff,

22:03.697 --> 22:07.492
32 minutes past the hour,
liftoff on Apollo 11.

22:50.160 --> 22:52.078
I do okay?

22:52.079 --> 22:53.622
Are you kidding me?

23:16.853 --> 23:18.146
This is nice.

23:19.773 --> 23:22.609
- We should do this more.
- Yeah. In.

23:33.620 --> 23:34.996
You okay?

23:36.540 --> 23:37.624
Yeah.

24:25.380 --> 24:26.882
Stop.

24:34.639 --> 24:35.640
Fuck.

24:37.058 --> 24:38.560
Joel, what the fuck?

24:39.436 --> 24:41.187
Exactly. What the fuck?

24:41.188 --> 24:43.105
- Get outta here.
- No, wait.

24:43.106 --> 24:46.108
What-- what are you even doing here?
You're supposed to be on patrol.

24:46.109 --> 24:49.153
I came home early
to surprise you for your birthday.

24:49.154 --> 24:51.907
- Oh, yeah.
- Seventeen, by the way.

24:52.532 --> 24:54.409
Well, I'm 19, so.

24:56.203 --> 24:57.454
I'm gonna go.

24:59.998 --> 25:02.292
- Fuck is that?
- Fuck.

25:05.337 --> 25:07.338
It's not done yet,
it's gonna look better when I fill in--

25:07.339 --> 25:08.715
- Leave.
- Right.

25:19.309 --> 25:21.520
So, all the teenage shit all at once, huh?

25:22.854 --> 25:26.024
Drugs, and tattoos, and sex.

25:26.608 --> 25:29.319
Experimenting with girls?

25:30.529 --> 25:33.740
It wasn't sex,
and it wasn't a fucking experiment.

25:36.743 --> 25:38.203
You don't know what you're sayin'.

25:39.955 --> 25:41.915
We'll discuss this later,
when you're yourself.

26:33.008 --> 26:35.384
- The hell are you doing?
- Moving into the garage.

26:35.385 --> 26:37.596
The hell you are. Ellie, let go.

26:38.305 --> 26:40.139
It's the middle of the night.
It's pissin' rain out there.

26:40.140 --> 26:41.849
Now, get this back on the bed.

26:41.850 --> 26:43.726
There's no heat
or running water in the garage.

26:43.727 --> 26:45.979
- You can't stay there.
- Okay, fine.

26:47.439 --> 26:49.566
Okay, you want to have
this conversation? Fine.

26:50.692 --> 26:52.568
You may not like the rules,
but this is my house.

26:52.569 --> 26:56.363
No, it isn't. You don't own it.
They gave it to you.

26:56.364 --> 26:58.198
Sorry, to us.

26:58.199 --> 26:59.993
You don't own anything.

27:11.171 --> 27:13.255
Look, I'm sorry that I got a tattoo,

27:13.256 --> 27:16.259
and smoked weed,
and fooled around with a girl.

27:18.345 --> 27:19.679
Except, I'm not.

27:22.724 --> 27:23.850
Maybe...

27:28.271 --> 27:30.440
Maybe it's a good thing for you
to have your own space.

27:32.984 --> 27:34.443
Just give me a few days

27:34.444 --> 27:36.363
and let me fix things up
a little out there.

27:38.573 --> 27:39.574
Okay.

27:43.453 --> 27:44.454
Come on.

28:01.471 --> 28:02.471
Thanks.

28:02.472 --> 28:03.556
Sure.

28:06.976 --> 28:08.144
Can I see?

28:14.526 --> 28:16.528
- Did it hurt?
- Yeah.

28:19.072 --> 28:20.490
But kinda good.

28:24.202 --> 28:25.704
It's actually not bad.

28:27.038 --> 28:31.334
Better than the one I made
on your guitar anyway.

28:37.465 --> 28:39.300
I never did ask.
What is it with the moths?

28:42.345 --> 28:43.637
Nothing. Just--

28:43.638 --> 28:47.182
I just read about them
in a book on dreams and stuff.

28:47.183 --> 28:48.892
It's kind of symbolic.

28:48.893 --> 28:50.395
Oh, right.

28:52.439 --> 28:57.360
Yeah, like change and growin' and such.

29:01.322 --> 29:02.490
It's late.

29:03.283 --> 29:04.284
Yeah.

29:05.994 --> 29:06.995
Well, good night.

29:08.329 --> 29:09.330
Night.

29:28.475 --> 29:29.517
Hey.

29:32.270 --> 29:35.857
You guys study dreams and stuff, right?

29:37.317 --> 29:41.362
Is there a "Doctor Is In" sign on me
like Lucy from fuckin' Peanuts?

29:44.407 --> 29:49.870
Yes, some doctors studied dreams.
The dumb ones, mostly.

29:49.871 --> 29:51.122
So, a moth.

29:52.207 --> 29:55.210
That probably means change and growth?

29:55.960 --> 29:57.629
No, that would be a butterfly.

29:59.380 --> 30:00.839
So, what's a moth?

30:00.840 --> 30:02.050
Death.

30:03.384 --> 30:04.844
If you believe in that shit.

30:14.813 --> 30:15.814
Why?

31:19.085 --> 31:21.462
Okay, so I've been thinking,

31:22.589 --> 31:27.093
or wondering--
no, thinking for a while now

31:28.094 --> 31:30.263
about Salt Lake City.

31:32.015 --> 31:33.808
I just want to understand it.

31:35.810 --> 31:38.563
So, I wrote down some questions.

31:39.856 --> 31:40.857
Okay?

31:43.276 --> 31:44.277
Okay.

31:53.202 --> 31:58.373
One, if the Fireflies
spotted us a mile from the hospital,

31:58.374 --> 32:01.502
how did they get surprised
by an entire group of Raiders?

32:05.423 --> 32:07.007
Two.

32:07.008 --> 32:10.260
If the Raiders could
kill all those soldiers,

32:10.261 --> 32:14.181
and Marlene,
and you had to carry me the whole time,

32:14.182 --> 32:15.683
how did we get away?

32:17.268 --> 32:19.645
Three, if there are dozens
of immune people,

32:19.646 --> 32:21.648
why hasn't anyone heard--

32:24.192 --> 32:25.193
Ellie?

32:26.611 --> 32:27.862
Coming.

32:35.328 --> 32:37.162
Already dressed.

32:37.163 --> 32:38.997
I figured I'd be waking you up.

32:38.998 --> 32:41.459
Nope. I had trouble sleeping.

32:42.752 --> 32:45.837
Well, guess what? That works out great
for your birthday present.

32:45.838 --> 32:48.299
You're 19 and you've been patient.

32:49.467 --> 32:51.343
So, I told 'em I was okay with it.

32:51.344 --> 32:54.305
- With what?
- Your first patrol.

32:56.766 --> 32:58.559
- I'll grab my coat.
- And a gun.

33:11.030 --> 33:14.574
So, what's the record for number of kills
on a training run?

33:14.575 --> 33:18.830
Zero. This is the safest trail we got.
Gotta start easy.

33:19.497 --> 33:20.873
Great. Happy birthday to me.

33:22.083 --> 33:24.918
- Come on, binoculars.
- Why? There's nothing out here.

33:24.919 --> 33:27.338
I know, but this is about
learnin' the ropes.

33:28.256 --> 33:30.049
So, pretend, okay?

33:32.343 --> 33:34.845
It's part of the rules.
You stick with your partner,

33:34.846 --> 33:37.557
scan the countryside,
be ready for anything.

33:38.099 --> 33:39.475
- Oh, shit.
- What?

33:41.227 --> 33:43.855
There's a little squirrel
fucking a big squirrel!

33:44.856 --> 33:46.149
We should probably report that.

33:48.609 --> 33:50.278
Fine, we'll skip the scannin' for now.

33:54.949 --> 33:56.908
But this is nice, right?

33:56.909 --> 33:59.912
Reminds me of the old days,
just you and me on the trail.

34:00.997 --> 34:02.914
I know you got stuff going on,
but it'd be nice

34:02.915 --> 34:05.500
if we could do
this kind of thing more often.

34:05.501 --> 34:06.794
Spend time together.

34:10.089 --> 34:11.090
Yeah.

34:15.803 --> 34:17.721
- You okay?
- Yeah.

34:17.722 --> 34:19.431
- It's just, you look...
- No, I--

34:19.432 --> 34:21.308
- There's nothin' on your mind?
- No, nothing.

34:21.309 --> 34:23.436
Cache Creek, this is Jackson. Come in.

34:26.898 --> 34:29.691
- Go for Cache Creek.
- Infected north of Pinnacle.

34:29.692 --> 34:32.612
Eugene and Adam need backup.
You're the closest we've got.

34:33.529 --> 34:36.239
I'll be there in ten.
Tell them to dig in.

34:36.240 --> 34:37.657
- Go back to Jackson.
- No.

34:37.658 --> 34:39.493
Ellie, it's not safe. Go back.

34:39.494 --> 34:43.206
I'm not your fucking kid, Joel.
I'm your partner. We stick together.

35:16.364 --> 35:19.158
We'll hike down from here.
Faster than the switchback.

35:56.487 --> 35:58.155
You remember what I taught you?

35:58.156 --> 35:59.782
I'm your back. You're mine.

36:35.735 --> 36:36.861
Come on.

37:05.139 --> 37:06.474
Oh, shit. Eugene.

37:07.308 --> 37:08.309
Ellie.

37:13.397 --> 37:14.565
You clean?

37:19.487 --> 37:20.488
No.

37:25.117 --> 37:26.701
- Are there any more?
- Joel.

37:26.702 --> 37:28.663
Are there any more?

37:29.413 --> 37:30.873
Other than me?

37:34.377 --> 37:35.378
No.

37:37.546 --> 37:40.257
Okay, okay. Look.

37:40.258 --> 37:43.301
Please, I figure I got about an hour.

37:43.302 --> 37:45.971
So, this is what we do.
We go back to the gate.

37:45.972 --> 37:50.475
They let Gail out,
keeping her at a safe distance, of course.

37:50.476 --> 37:52.728
And I say

37:53.854 --> 37:55.064
goodbye.

37:56.691 --> 37:57.858
We can't do that.

37:58.859 --> 38:00.486
Yes, we can.

38:05.116 --> 38:07.994
- Yes, we can.
- You're empty.

38:12.456 --> 38:13.790
No.

38:13.791 --> 38:16.459
Joel, I gotta go back. I gotta see her.

38:16.460 --> 38:20.089
I got things I gotta tell her.

38:22.842 --> 38:24.384
Things.

38:24.385 --> 38:26.512
- You don't understand.
- I do.

38:27.513 --> 38:29.556
But we have rules, and it can't happen.

38:29.557 --> 38:30.641
Wait.

38:34.270 --> 38:35.688
Hold out your hand.

38:41.819 --> 38:42.903
Hold out your hand.

38:46.198 --> 38:49.452
Now, count slowly,
clearly, from one to ten.

38:51.662 --> 38:54.831
One, two, three,

38:54.832 --> 38:56.833
four, five,

38:56.834 --> 39:00.211
six, seven, eight,

39:00.212 --> 39:02.840
nine, ten.

39:03.841 --> 39:07.094
He has time.
We tie him up and we bring him back.

39:09.638 --> 39:11.640
Joel, let him see his fucking wife.

39:12.933 --> 39:14.185
Please.

39:22.109 --> 39:24.110
Get the horses, bring them down the trail.

39:24.111 --> 39:26.155
I'll start walkin' with him,
we'll meet up with you.

39:39.585 --> 39:40.669
I promise.

39:50.763 --> 39:52.181
Go ahead, ten feet.

39:53.265 --> 39:54.266
Thank you.

40:21.752 --> 40:24.922
It makes you cold. The Cordyceps.

40:26.507 --> 40:28.342
I didn't expect that.

40:33.639 --> 40:35.599
Which way?

40:39.186 --> 40:40.271
Head right.

40:59.957 --> 41:01.792
It's beautiful.

41:11.927 --> 41:14.138
I need you to not turn around.

41:15.306 --> 41:16.890
No.

41:16.891 --> 41:18.391
You can't--

41:18.392 --> 41:20.351
you can't do this to me.

41:20.352 --> 41:21.604
Joel.

41:22.688 --> 41:25.315
If you have last words for her,
I'll pass them along.

41:25.316 --> 41:26.984
Last words for her?

41:28.027 --> 41:29.195
No, no, I need...

41:29.904 --> 41:31.572
I need her last words!

41:32.698 --> 41:34.116
For me!

41:36.911 --> 41:38.204
I'm dying.

41:39.038 --> 41:40.998
I'm terrified. I...

41:46.587 --> 41:47.880
I don't need a view.

41:51.300 --> 41:52.676
I need Gail.

41:55.304 --> 41:57.348
To see her face. Please.

41:58.516 --> 42:00.851
Please let that be the last thing I see.

42:06.524 --> 42:07.983
If you love someone,

42:10.986 --> 42:12.571
you can always see their face.

42:49.900 --> 42:51.193
I see her.

43:45.247 --> 43:46.415
I'm sorry.

44:08.604 --> 44:10.814
I'm gonna radio ahead and let them know.

44:12.941 --> 44:19.907
When we get there, I'll tell Gail
what she needs to know, and nothin' more.

44:21.450 --> 44:22.868
It's the right thing to do.

44:26.580 --> 44:27.581
Ellie.

44:32.127 --> 44:33.545
I had no choice.

45:15.754 --> 45:18.090
He was bit when we found him.

45:19.800 --> 45:20.926
And...

45:22.761 --> 45:24.847
Well, he wanted to tell you
that he loved you.

45:28.600 --> 45:32.019
And he wished he could say goodbye
to you in person

45:32.020 --> 45:34.021
but he didn't wanna put you in danger.

45:34.022 --> 45:35.441
No, no.

45:36.191 --> 45:38.694
And he wasn't scared. He...

45:39.737 --> 45:41.155
He was brave.

45:44.366 --> 45:45.951
And he ended it himself.

45:59.381 --> 46:00.799
That's not what happened.

46:06.764 --> 46:09.558
He begged to see you.
He had time.

46:10.267 --> 46:12.685
Joel promised to take him to you.

46:12.686 --> 46:14.271
He promised us both.

46:17.232 --> 46:20.068
And then, Joel shot him in the head.

46:30.788 --> 46:31.955
That's...

46:35.334 --> 46:37.585
Get away. Please.

46:37.586 --> 46:39.671
Get away from me, please.

46:46.094 --> 46:47.429
You swore.

46:56.021 --> 46:57.564
No.

47:48.907 --> 47:50.242
That was good, yeah?

47:51.660 --> 47:53.077
Oh, okay.

47:53.078 --> 47:55.496
Yeah, he's fallin' apart.
I'm gonna get him to bed.

47:55.497 --> 47:58.124
- You're gonna miss the countdown.
- I'll come back after.

47:58.125 --> 48:00.084
Okay.
The next one is a little slower.

48:00.085 --> 48:01.794
Save me some of that.

48:01.795 --> 48:03.087
Say goodnight to Uncle Grumpy.

48:03.088 --> 48:05.798
Goodnight, Uncle Grumpy.

48:05.799 --> 48:08.385
- Night, kiddo.
- See you next year.

48:08.927 --> 48:10.429
See you next year.

48:20.814 --> 48:22.024
You okay?

48:24.151 --> 48:25.319
Yeah, I'm fine.

48:27.237 --> 48:29.947
What I said today
about you being a refugee

48:29.948 --> 48:31.908
probably came off as ungrateful.

48:31.909 --> 48:34.995
- No, it's okay.
- Well, I am grateful.

48:35.913 --> 48:38.164
You mean a lot to us.
To all of us.

48:38.165 --> 48:40.333
But especially to me and Tommy.

48:40.334 --> 48:44.171
What I'm trying to say is,
Uncle Grumpy is family.

48:45.255 --> 48:49.259
And family helps each other out,
if you need it.

48:52.346 --> 48:54.556
Hey, it's a family event.

48:55.849 --> 48:56.850
Sorry.

48:59.019 --> 49:00.686
Sorry.

49:00.687 --> 49:03.064
In a church. Dykes.

49:03.065 --> 49:04.690
- Fuck did you just say?
- Ellie, no.

49:04.691 --> 49:05.776
Ellie, hey. No.

49:07.945 --> 49:09.488
You get the hell out of here.

49:10.197 --> 49:11.823
Seth. Let's...

49:12.407 --> 49:16.703
Let's take a walk.
Come on. Let's go.

49:19.039 --> 49:20.082
Are you okay?

49:21.416 --> 49:22.876
What is wrong with you?

49:26.755 --> 49:29.424
I don't need your fucking help.

49:37.975 --> 49:38.976
Right.

51:44.559 --> 51:45.811
What are you drinking?

51:47.771 --> 51:48.772
Coffee.

51:49.773 --> 51:50.899
Where'd you get it?

51:53.360 --> 51:55.362
The people that came through last week.

51:56.863 --> 52:00.367
I'm a little embarrassed
for what I traded to get it, but...

52:01.326 --> 52:02.786
it's not bad.

52:13.213 --> 52:14.840
I had Seth under control.

52:17.551 --> 52:19.677
Yeah, I know.

52:19.678 --> 52:22.597
And I don't wanna ever hear
about you taking me off patrol again.

52:25.267 --> 52:26.268
Okay.

52:34.025 --> 52:35.402
So, Dina.

52:38.029 --> 52:40.281
Is she your girlfriend now?

52:40.282 --> 52:42.659
No. No, she...

52:44.828 --> 52:47.747
It was just one kiss.
Didn't mean anything.

52:50.167 --> 52:51.668
I don't know why she did that.

52:54.212 --> 52:55.213
But...

52:57.090 --> 52:58.216
you do like her?

53:03.221 --> 53:04.764
I'm so stupid.

53:08.393 --> 53:11.354
Look, I don't know what
Dina's intentions are, but...

53:15.275 --> 53:16.902
well, she'd be lucky to have you.

53:20.572 --> 53:22.199
You're such an asshole.

53:27.704 --> 53:28.997
You lied to me.

53:30.790 --> 53:35.170
You looked me in the eyes and you lied,
and it was the same face.

53:36.421 --> 53:38.465
Same fucking look.

53:43.178 --> 53:44.804
But I think I knew already.

53:47.515 --> 53:49.226
I knew this whole time.

53:55.732 --> 53:57.651
So, I'm gonna give you one last chance.

54:00.028 --> 54:02.030
Tell me what happened with the Fireflies.

54:03.615 --> 54:06.493
If you lie to me again, we're done.

54:16.586 --> 54:18.088
Were there other immune people?

54:33.937 --> 54:35.522
Were there Raiders?

54:45.031 --> 54:46.616
Could they have made a cure?

55:08.305 --> 55:09.597
Did you--

55:16.187 --> 55:17.647
And Marlene?

55:27.198 --> 55:28.450
Making a cure

55:31.369 --> 55:32.620
would've killed you.

55:34.331 --> 55:36.165
Then, I was supposed to die.

55:36.166 --> 55:39.126
That was my purpose.
My life would have fucking mattered!

55:39.127 --> 55:40.837
But you took that from me!

55:41.838 --> 55:43.548
You took it from everyone.

55:45.675 --> 55:46.676
Yes.

55:49.971 --> 55:51.431
And I'll pay the price

55:53.016 --> 55:55.060
because you're gonna turn away from me.

56:00.148 --> 56:03.026
But if somehow I had a second chance
at that moment,

56:06.988 --> 56:08.448
I would do it all over again.

56:11.701 --> 56:13.495
Because you're selfish.

56:14.871 --> 56:16.539
Because I love you.

56:22.545 --> 56:23.797
In a way you...

56:25.632 --> 56:27.759
you can't understand.

56:30.678 --> 56:31.971
Maybe you never will.

56:35.475 --> 56:37.227
But if that day should come,

56:40.021 --> 56:42.065
if you should ever have one of your own,

56:48.655 --> 56:49.739
well, then...

56:54.035 --> 56:55.870
I hope you do a little better than me.

57:13.471 --> 57:15.890
I don't think I can forgive you for this.

57:25.567 --> 57:27.277
But I would like to try.
